In article <BxJqxB.EyG@usenet.ucs.indiana.edu>, ahabig@bigbang.astro.indiana.edu (Alec Habig) writes...
> I've got the mail daemon working on my UNIX system, but would like to make
> it work on VMS too.  Has anyone had any luck with porting this feasture of
> nethack to a VMS box?

     The mail daemon and scrolls of mail are already supported in the VMS
port.  Rather than periodically polling the user's mailbox (or mail spool
directory or whatever), what it does is capture incoming broadcast messages
(such as "new mail from so-and-so").  The mail daemon delivers a scroll of
mail and when the scroll is read, the text of the broadcast is shown.  (You
can then use '!' to escape into a subprocess to read your mail if desired.)
Under 3.1 it will attempt to distinguish between differents types of
broadcasts and provide the user with the opportunity to spawn a command
for responding when the player reads the scroll, closer to the current
Unix behavior.  Non-MAIL and non-PHONE broadcasts will still be delivered
by the daemon but no scroll will be created in those cases.

     To enable this feature, just #define MAIL in vmsconf.h prior to
building the program (note that that is already the default).  There have
been reports of broadcast trapping not working for some users.  So far no
one has figured out why.  (It works fine for me. :-)

